# Cloudflare Pages routing.
#
# Single-page-app fallback. The site uses a history router, so
# /journeys/spiti-circuit is a real URL with no file behind it. Without this,
# Pages returns its own 404 for every deep link, shared link and refresh — the
# dev server and Vercel's Vite preset were both doing this for us silently.
#
# 200, not 301: the page is served at the requested path rather than
# redirected to /, so the address bar keeps the URL the router reads. Static
# assets match before this rule, so it only catches routes.
/*    /index.html   200

# A NOTE ON /api/* — DO NOT ADD A RULE FOR IT HERE.
#
# An earlier version tried "/api/*  /api-offline.json  404" so that calls
# made before the backend exists would fail cleanly. Pages ignores it:
# _redirects supports 200 and the 30x codes only, so the line is dropped and
# the catch-all above answers /api/v1/... with index.html and a 200.
#
# It does not matter, because the forms POST, and Cloudflare answers a POST to
# a static path with 405 — so a submission fails visibly instead of being
# quietly swallowed. Tested, not assumed.
#
# The right fix is to set VITE_API_URL on the Pages project to the API's own
# host, even before that host exists. The request then leaves this origin
# entirely, fetch rejects, and lib/api.js shows "We could not reach our
# servers" rather than a generic server error.
